cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use cp_parallel in your work, please cite it using the metadata below,
  and also cite CellProfiler, which cp_parallel runs (see "references").
title: "cp_parallel: run CellProfiler headless in parallel across plates or wells"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jenna
    family-names: Tomkinson
    affiliation: University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus
  - given-names: Dave
    family-names: Bunten
    affiliation: University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus
  - given-names: Mike
    family-names: Lippincott
    affiliation: University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus
repository-code: "https://github.com/WayScience/CP_Parallel"
abstract: >-
  cp_parallel is a small Python package that runs CellProfiler headless on
  multiple plates (or wells) in parallel, writing one log file per run. It
  supports plate- and well-level grouping, LoadData CSVs, batch processing by
  image-set range, and running inside Apptainer/Singularity containers on HPC.
keywords:
  - CellProfiler
  - Cell Painting
  - image analysis
  - parallel processing
  - high-content screening
license: BSD-3-Clause
references:
  - type: article
    title: "CellProfiler 4: improvements in speed, utility and usability"
    authors:
      - given-names: David R.
        family-names: Stirling
      - given-names: Madison J.
        family-names: Swain-Bowden
      - given-names: Alice M.
        family-names: Lucas
      - given-names: Anne E.
        family-names: Carpenter
      - given-names: Beth A.
        family-names: Cimini
      - given-names: Allen
        family-names: Goodman
    journal: BMC Bioinformatics
    volume: 22
    start: 433
    year: 2021
    doi: 10.1186/s12859-021-04344-9
